  "notes": {
    "raw": "Phase change: 1936 K, melting point of Lu; $\\Delta H^{\\circ} = 4.457$ kcal/mol. \nHeat capacity (cal/mol·K) and enthalpy (kcal/mol) equations: \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-2000 K:</td><td> $Cp^o = 8.437 + 0.350x10^{-3}T - 0.886x10^5T^{-2}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $H^o - H_{2,9,8}^o = 8.437x10^{-3}T + 0.175x10^{-6}T^2 + 0.886x10^2T^{-1} - 2.828$ </td></tr></table>\nFormation equations (kcal/mol): \n<table><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">298.15-1936 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = -0.269 + 0.925 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 1.831 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 195.500 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = -0.269 - 0.925 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} + 1.831 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 97.750 \\text{T}^{-1} - 14.947 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr><tr><td rowspan=\"2\">1936-2000 K:</td><td> $\\Delta Hf^{\\circ} = 3.390 - 6.628 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} - 0.076 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 66.000 \\text{T}^{-1}$ </td></tr><tr><td> $\\Delta Gf^{\\circ} = 3.390 + 6.628 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T} \\ln \\text{T} + 0.076 \\times 10^{-6} \\text{T}^{2} + 33.000 \\text{T}^{-1} - 70.588 \\times 10^{-3} \\text{T}$ </td></tr></table>\nSource: Data from Pedley (396). ",
    "lines_raw": [
